  "enhanced_information": "Adalimumab is an antibody against TNF-alpha and is a fully human monoclonal antibody, not an antibody against completely human TNF. Abatacept inhibits T-cell activation by binding to CD80/86 on antigen-presenting cells, but it does not prevent the maturation of B lymphocytes to plasma cells. Anakinra is a recombinant antagonist of IL-1 receptors, not IL-6 receptors. Etanercept is a fusion protein of the TNF receptor and the Fc portion of IgG1, not a chimeric monoclonal antibody."
